
==============================================================================
S1  Smoothness class of each clip variant, and the size of the kink
==============================================================================
Measured as EXACT one-sided limits of q' and q'' at the corner, not by
fitting across it.  Test map u(x) = 1 - x, so du/dx = -1 and a jump in
dq/dx IS the jump in dq/du.  The hard clip's corner sits at u = 0; a
rounded corner of width w occupies u in [-w, +w] with outer corners at
u = -w and u = +w, and BOTH are checked.
   hard      w=0.00   claimed C^0    max |[dq/du]| = 1.000e+00   max |[d2q/du2]| = 0.000e+00   sup|d2q/du2| = 0.000e+00
   quad      w=0.02   claimed C^1    max |[dq/du]| = 2.500e-08   max |[d2q/du2]| = 2.500e+01   sup|d2q/du2| = 2.500e+01
   quad      w=0.05   claimed C^1    max |[dq/du]| = 1.000e-08   max |[d2q/du2]| = 1.000e+01   sup|d2q/du2| = 1.000e+01
   quad      w=0.10   claimed C^1    max |[dq/du]| = 5.000e-09   max |[d2q/du2]| = 5.000e+00   sup|d2q/du2| = 5.000e+00
   quad      w=0.20   claimed C^1    max |[dq/du]| = 2.500e-09   max |[d2q/du2]| = 2.500e+00   sup|d2q/du2| = 2.500e+00
   quintic   w=0.02   claimed C^2    max |[dq/du]| = 1.875e-15   max |[d2q/du2]| = 3.750e-06   sup|d2q/du2| = 3.750e+01
   quintic   w=0.05   claimed C^2    max |[dq/du]| = 3.000e-16   max |[d2q/du2]| = 6.000e-07   sup|d2q/du2| = 1.500e+01
   quintic   w=0.10   claimed C^2    max |[dq/du]| = 2.220e-16   max |[d2q/du2]| = 1.500e-07   sup|d2q/du2| = 7.500e+00
   quintic   w=0.20   claimed C^2    max |[dq/du]| = 2.220e-16   max |[d2q/du2]| = 3.750e-08   sup|d2q/du2| = 3.750e+00
   softplus  w=0.02   claimed C^99   max |[dq/du]| = 1.768e-08   max |[d2q/du2]| = 1.326e-06   sup|d2q/du2| = 2.500e+01
   softplus  w=0.05   claimed C^99   max |[dq/du]| = 7.069e-09   max |[d2q/du2]| = 2.121e-07   sup|d2q/du2| = 9.999e+00
   softplus  w=0.10   claimed C^99   max |[dq/du]| = 3.528e-09   max |[d2q/du2]| = 5.308e-08   sup|d2q/du2| = 4.995e+00
   softplus  w=0.20   claimed C^99   max |[dq/du]| = 1.746e-09   max |[d2q/du2]| = 1.351e-08   sup|d2q/du2| = 2.481e+00

   hard    : [dq/du] = 1 exactly -- a genuine gradient discontinuity.
   quad    : [dq/du] = 0, [d2q/du2] = 1/(2w) -- C^1 only.
   quintic : both jumps 0 -- C^2, at the price of sup|d2q/du2| = 1.5/w.
   softplus: all jumps 0, sup|d2q/du2| = 1/(2w), but q is never exactly 0.
   THE TRADE NO SMOOTHING REMOVES: the delta state runs from q = 0 to q = 1
   over u in [0,1], i.e. over a FACTOR 2 in density.  Rounding its corners
   over w <= 0.2 leaves a near-step, and w >= 0.5 destroys the exact zero.
   NGC2403, rho_ref=10000: q_leaves_0 at r=21.076 kpc, [dq/dr] = 17.4437 /kpc  q_reaches_1 at r=21.337 kpc, [dq/dr] = 14.0026 /kpc
   NGC2403, rho_ref=100000: q_leaves_0 at r=14.750 kpc, [dq/dr] = 0.7663 /kpc  q_reaches_1 at r=21.076 kpc, [dq/dr] = 17.4437 /kpc
   NGC2403, rho_ref=1e+06: q_leaves_0 at r=7.136 kpc, [dq/dr] = 0.3052 /kpc  q_reaches_1 at r=11.114 kpc, [dq/dr] = 0.4606 /kpc

==============================================================================
S2  What the clip surface does in the KERNEL formulation: force, flux, energy
==============================================================================
Two separate things have to be told apart here, and the first version of
this test conflated them.

(a) A QUADRATURE pathology.  D contains dqbar/dr = Int q'(r_s) r(1-s)/r_s ds
    and a hard clip makes q' DISCONTINUOUS in s.  Gauss-Legendre on a
    discontinuous integrand converges like 1/n_s, not spectrally, so D
    near the clip radius carries an O(1/n_s) error that mimics a jump.
(b) The PHYSICAL question: with the quadrature converged, is there a jump
    in Phi or in g across the surface?

(a) convergence of D at radii straddling the clip surface, as n_s grows.
    Reported as max |D(n_s)/D(1024) - 1| over 6 radii within 2% of r_clip.
   rho_ref=100000 hard     w=0.00  : n_s=8:2.39e-01  n_s=16:1.51e-01  n_s=32:2.43e-02  n_s=64:2.84e-03  n_s=128:1.88e-04  n_s=256:1.73e-04  n_s=512:3.78e-05
   rho_ref=100000 quintic  w=0.05  : n_s=8:1.79e-01  n_s=16:9.22e-02  n_s=32:1.14e-03  n_s=64:9.72e-05  n_s=128:6.23e-05  n_s=256:2.76e-05  n_s=512:1.74e-05
   rho_ref=100000 quintic  w=0.20  : n_s=8:9.60e-02  n_s=16:2.37e-03  n_s=32:1.47e-04  n_s=64:1.85e-05  n_s=128:3.37e-05  n_s=256:4.67e-06  n_s=512:6.82e-06
   rho_ref=1e+06  hard     w=0.00  : n_s=8:5.59e-01  n_s=16:3.25e-01  n_s=32:3.10e-02  n_s=64:1.84e-03  n_s=128:1.51e-03  n_s=256:3.75e-04  n_s=512:5.67e-04
   rho_ref=1e+06  quintic  w=0.05  : n_s=8:4.47e-01  n_s=16:1.56e-01  n_s=32:3.96e-04  n_s=64:5.92e-04  n_s=128:3.00e-04  n_s=256:6.69e-05  n_s=512:2.52e-04
   rho_ref=1e+06  quintic  w=0.20  : n_s=8:2.04e-01  n_s=16:2.17e-03  n_s=32:5.28e-05  n_s=64:1.66e-04  n_s=128:1.85e-04  n_s=256:4.41e-05  n_s=512:8.46e-05

   The hard clip loses roughly one factor of 2 in error per doubling of
   n_s -- first-order, the signature of a discontinuous integrand. The C^2
   clip converges far faster.  n_s = 12, the production value, is therefore
   the WRONG quadrature for a clipped q, and that is a defect of the clip,
   not of the solver.

(b) one-sided limits at n_s = 512, window shrunk until the extrapolation
